#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kiriki; is an addictive and fun dice game for &kde;, designed to be played "
"by as many as six players. Participants have to collect points by rolling "
"five dice for up to three times per single turn. Each roll generates a "
"specific combination of numbers which the player is free to either accept or "
"decline. However, each specific combination of numbers can be accepted only "
"once. After thirteen turns the game ends and the scores are compared. The "
"player with the largest amount of points wins the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Objective:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Earn more score points then either of the opponents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once &kiriki; starts, it right away gives out the first combination for the "
"player one. If you are the player one, then it is now your turn, otherwise "
"you will have to wait until all other players make their moves."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:71 index.docbook:73 index.docbook:77 index.docbook:79
#: index.docbook:255 index.docbook:257 index.docbook:259 index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Note:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, unless the game settings have been changed, and in single player "
"mode, the first player is controlled by human (you), while all other five "
"players are controlled by Artificial Intelligence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once it is your turn, the first thing you should do is examine the current "
"roll. Each of the five dice on the left hand side of the game screen has a "
"specific value. Check the sequence to see if these values form any of the "
"score patterns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The detailed description of the score patterns can be found in the <link "
"linkend=\"rules_and_tips\">‘Game Rules, Strategies and Tips’</link> section "
"of this docbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that the combination can match more then one score pattern. In "
"this case you will have to determine which score pattern will result in "
"greater points for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case the current sequence matches no score pattern, or matches a score "
"pattern you have already used up, you have two more rolls to fix the "
"situation. To use your second (third) roll select the dice you are not "
"satisfied with by clicking on them with your mouse and click ‘Roll’ button "
"located right under the dice. This will cause the dice in question to "
"reroll, thus changing their values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have done the third reroll you must choose the score pattern which "
"feats the dice sequence on hand. If none of the score patterns feet the "
"sequence - you can either use ‘Chance’ score pattern, or just select any "
"score pattern on your scoreboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select score pattern that does not feet current dice sequence, the "
"score pattern you select will become void and of zero value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As soon as you choose the score pattern its value updates to reflect the "
"dice sequence you currently have."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The detailed description of the score pattern values can be found in the "
"<link linkend=\"rules_and_tips\">‘Game Rules, Strategies and Tips’</link> "
"section of this docbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Right after that your turn ends and the next participant’s turn begins. This "
"sequence repeats some thirteen times and then the game ends, the scores are "
"calculated and the high scores are awarded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules, Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:85
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Rules"
msgid "Game Rules"
msgstr "Règlas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kiriki; score board is divided into fourteen different lines. Each line "
"holds a single score pattern and the players' score earned for a roll "
"matching the pattern. The score pattern of each line is calculated as "
"follows: <itemizedlist> <listitem><para>1s: Sum of all dice valued ‘1’."
"<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '14112'. The sum is: "
"'3'='1'+'1'+'1'. Dice on display: '51111'. The sum is: '4'='1'+'1'+'1'+'1'.</"
"para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>2s: Sum of all dice valued "
"‘2’.<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '22422'. The sum is: "
"'8'='2'+'2'+'2'+'2'. Dice on display: '42322'. The sum is: '6'='2'+'2'+'2'.</"
"para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>3s: Sum of all dice valued "
"‘3’.<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '34132'. The sum is: "
"'6'='3'+'3'. Dice on display: '33333'. The sum is: '15'='3'+'3'+'3'+'3'+'3'."
"</para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>4s: Sum of all dice valued "
"‘4’.<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '14142'. The sum is: "
"'8'='4'+'4'. Dice on display: '41414'. The sum is: '12'='4'+'4'+'4'.</para></"
"note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>5s: Sum of all dice valued ‘5’."
"<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '15155'. The sum is: "
"'15'='5'+'5'+'5'. Dice on display: '51555'. The sum is: '20'='5'+'5'+'5'+'5'."
"</para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>6s: Sum of all dice valued "
"‘6’.<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '66616'. The sum is: "
"'24'='6'+'6'+'6'+'6'. Dice on display: '61616'. The sum is: '18'='6'+'6'+'6'."
"</para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>Bonus if > 62: Player is "
"awarded an additional 35 points if the summarized value of all the field "
"above is greater then 62 points.</para></listitem> <listitem><para>Upper "
"Total: It is not a playable field, but only a summary of all the fields "
"above.</para></listitem> <listitem><para>3 of a Kind: Summarized value of "
"three dice bearing the same kind.<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on "
"display: '14121'. The sum is: '3'='1'+'1'+'1'. Dice on display: '55151'. The "
"sum is: '15'='5'+'5'+'5'.</para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>4 "
"of a Kind: Summarized value of four dice bearing the same kind."
"<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '41444'. The sum is: "
"'16'='4'+'4'+'4'+'4'. Dice on display: '22522'. The sum is: "
"'8'='2'+'2'+'2'+'2'.</para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>Full "
"House: 25 points are awarded to the player if the round results in three "
"dice of a kind and a pair.<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on "
"display: '11212'. Dice on display: '53353'.</para></note></para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para>Small Straight: 30 points are awarded to the player if the "
"round results in four dice of sequential value.<note><title>Example:</"
"title><para>Dice on display: '14312'. The sequence is: '1','2','3','4'. Dice "
"on display: '51643'. The sequence is: '3','4','5','6'.</para></note></para></"
"listitem> <listitem><para>Large Straight: 30 points are awarded to the "
"player if the round results in five dice of sequential value."
"<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '34152'. The sequence "
"is: '1','2','3','4','5'. Dice on display: '53264'. The sequence is: "
"'2','3','4','5','6'.</para></note></para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para>&kiriki;: 50 points and a additional turn are awarded to the "
"player if the round results in five dice of the same value."
"<note><title>Example:</title><para>Dice on display: '11111'. Dice on "
"display: '33333'.</para></note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>Chance: "
"Summarized value of all the dice currently on display.<note><title>Example:</"
"title><para>Dice on display: '51143'. The sum is: '14'='5'+'1'+'1'+'4'+'3'. "
"Dice on display: '21526'. The sum is: '16'='2'+'1'+'5'+'2'+'6'.</para></"
"note></para></listitem> <listitem><para>Lower Total: It is not a playable "
"field, but only a summary of all the fields starting from '3 of a Kind' and "
"lower.</para></listitem> <listitem><para>Grand Total: It is not a playable "
"field, but only a sum of 'Upper Total' and 'Lower Total' fields.</para></"
"listitem> </itemizedlist> Other rules and constrains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "The entire game round is split into 13 turns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each player can do one to three rolls of dice per turn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the first roll is done, player can perform additional rolls for up to "
"two times (three rolls at all per turn)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Player is not obligated to perform additional rolls if the first roll brings "
"satisfactory results."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each additional roll may either involve all the dice, or only the selected "
"ones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Player can select the dice to be recast by clicking on them with the mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the dice have been recast their previous value is lost and only the new "
"value is valid."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The result of the roll is considered satisfactory if the values of the dice "
"on display can be put into one of the score patterns discussed above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each individual score pattern can only be used once per game per player. "
"Therefore, once the score pattern has been used by the player ‘X’ it can no "
"longer be used by that same player. However, another player ‘Y’ can still "
"use it, unless that same player ‘Y’ has used this same pattern up already."
msgstr ""

