msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Who made this game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "The kdegames team. You can find their website here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get cheatcodes?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can't get cheatcodes for KDE games."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I start a new game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To start a new game of &kiriki; use <link linkend=\"game-menu-new\">Game-"
">New</link> option on the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I pause the game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kiriki; does not time the gameplay and therefore needs no 'Pause' feature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the way this game looks. Can I?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "No. &kiriki; does not currently feature any themes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "I have made a mistake. Can I undo?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "No. &kiriki; has no 'Undo' option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use keyboard?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "No. The game of &kiriki; can not be played using keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "I can't figure out what to do here! Are there hints?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To learn about the game play rules and tactics please read <link linkend="
"\"rules_and_tips\">Game Rules, Strategies and Tips</link> section of this "
"docbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have to quit the game now, but I'm not finished yet. Can I save my "
"progress?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "No. There is no 'Save' feature in &kiriki;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where are the highscores?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To access the highscores dialog use <link linkend=\"game-menu-highscores"
"\">Game->Show High Scores...</link> option on the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the game configuration. Where do I go?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the game configuration please use the game configuration dialog "
"discussed in <link linkend=\"configuration\">Game Configuration</link> "
"section of this docbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the players' names. Where do I go?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the players' names please use the game configuration dialog "
"discussed in <link linkend=\"configuration\">Game Configuration</link> "
"section of this docbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I want to play &kiriki; with my friends. Where do I set who controls the "
"player?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the players' identities please use the game configuration dialog "
"discussed in <link linkend=\"configuration\">Game Configuration</link> "
"section of this docbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "The AI is too dam fast! I can't see what he's doing!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change Artificial Intelligence's speed of action please use the game "
"configuration dialog discussed in <link linkend=\"configuration\">Game "
"Configuration</link> section of this docbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kiriki; configuration dialog lets to you configure the number of "
"participants, to manage their identities, and their response times."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the response times for Artificial Intelligence driven players "
"only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Number of players: this field defines the number of players for &kiriki;. "
"The values allowed here range between two and six."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "The number of players can not be less then two."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"1.-6. Numbered fields are the identities of the participating players. You "
"can change their names as well as specify whether they will be human "
"controlled, or driven by the Artificial Intelligence. To define who controls "
"the player use a checkbox located on the right hand side, right next to the "
"name entry box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "The first player must always be human controlled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Delay between computers move (msec): lets you specify the delay between "
"Artificial Intelligence's turns. The value of this field is zero by default, "
"meaning that the Artificial Intelligence reacts instantaneously."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "The maximum value for this field is 999 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

